Author: ember arlynx <ember@lunar.town>
Date:   Thu Jun 25 09:10:43 2026 -0400

    fix(recursion engine): the DSU global-WitnessId(0) collapse + a next-row opening-schedule bug (2 genuine fixes; IVC height-1 residual still open)
    
    Toward closing dregg's IVC same-endpoint mixed-root (the un-forgeable-history floor). Two real, fork-test-green engine fixes:
    
    FIX 1 — the DSU global-WitnessId(0) collapse (the named diagnosis, codex-reviewed): in the lowerer
    (circuit/src/builder/compiler/lowerer/state.rs), a connect(a,b) with EXACTLY ONE side Const (the assert_zero(x) ==
    connect(x, ZERO) family; predicate a_is_const ^ b_is_const) is no longer fed to the union-find for value-bearing variants
    (Public|PrivateInput|Add|Sub|Mul|Div|HornerAcc|BoolCheck|MulAdd|NonPrimitiveOutput). A new pass emit_deferred_const_connects
    (mod.rs, after emit_operations) re-emits each as a per-target equality Op::mul_add(value, ZERO, const, value)
    (value*0+const==value <=> value==const) — codex chose MulAdd over a 2nd Op::Const (ConstAir treats every Op::Const as a
    creator; MulAdd flows through existing ALU bus accounting). So a created/exposed nonzero value keeps its OWN witness slot and
    a mismatch fails LOCALLY instead of clobbering the shared WitnessId(0). Eliminated the 219-member ZERO-class collapse. 3 fork
    tests asserting the old const-aliasing updated to the equality semantics.
    
    FIX 2 — recursive-verifier next-row opening schedule (surfaced once FIX 1 localized the conflict): the recursive batch-STARK
    verifier/generator unconditionally assumed zeta_next (next-row) openings exist for every AIR, but native prove_batch only
    opens at zeta_next when main/preprocessed_next_row_columns() are non-empty; single-row tables declare vec![] but the
    DynamicAirEntry + CircuitTableAir(s) wrappers didn't forward (BaseAir default = all columns) -> prover/verifier disagreed.
    Fixed across 7 files (dynamic_air, batch_stark_prover, proof, batch_stark, generation, traits/air, recursion) — gate zeta_next
    on the AIR's declarations both sides, mirroring native. Validated red-then-green (aggregation_different_shapes).
    
    Fork suite GREEN (p3-circuit 354/354, p3-circuit-prover 40+3, p3-recursion integration). NOT a complete IVC close: the heavy
    folds still fail on a SEPARATE, deeper residual — a height-1 (base-domain-1) W24 Poseidon2 perm table yields a genuinely-
    nonzero FRI reduced-opening (verifier.rs:1326, the reduced_openings height-1 ro==0 branch) asserted-zero in the recursive
    aggregation verifier, on the HONEST path (a correctness bug in the circuit-model of the opening schedule for a height-1-WITH-
    next-row matrix, NOT forgery detection). Coverage gap: no fork test aggregates an expose_claim/W24-Poseidon2-bearing proof.
    Next: a fork-level reproducer of the height-1 opening pairing vs native open_input. Fix lands in recursion/src/pcs/fri/
    verifier.rs open_input (~1062-1340) or batch_stark.rs per-matrix opening assembly.
    
    Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>

